// WHY THIS MODULE:
// Implements Lipi's bare-metal Linux multithreaded Stop-The-World (STW) Garbage Collector:
// 1. Lazy 256KB thread stack registry (4096 x 64B cache-line aligned ThreadSlots) via SYS_mmap.
// 2. Cooperative 1-instruction safepoint in _lipi_user_alloc + IN_SYSCALL tracking in _lipi_futex_wait.
// 3. Pure-kernel asynchronous SIGURG (23) preemption fallback (SYS_rt_sigaction + SYS_tgkill +
//    SYS_rt_sigreturn) with deadlock-freedom lock-bit guard ([slab+96] / [slab+88]) so tight spin
//    loops or raw blocking syscalls never deadlock STW GC.
// 4. Scans EVERY live thread's stack + pushed GPRs + kernel ucontext + dynamic RW globals span.
// 5. Zero overhead on single-threaded programs (_gc_active_threads == 0 fast path).
// ==============================================================================

